From 54d650be33bcba9f94cc6e7f6886e74aa3777893 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gf691271 <gf691271@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:21:12 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix: a stalled sync recovers by itself, the blob waits for
 the sync, heart rates above 127 stay positive

Four findings from the 2026-11-22 review, measured on 11-21.

1. The busy watchdog cleared the flag but did not bring the watch back. The 02:00 sync stalled
   (the fourth 0x07/0x0d got no answer), the watchdog cleared it at 02:28, and the 08:00 sync
   stalled again (0x07/0x0c got no answer at all). Only a phone restart at 11:54 recovered the
   link; on 11-18 a stall lasted 34 hours. The watchdog now also closes the socket, which sends
   the normal reconnect path, and after the reconnect asks for one fresh sync (at most one such
   resync per 30 minutes). It also measures by the wall clock: its "10 ticks" of 60 s took 27 and
   32 minutes in doze.

2. The sleep_data.bin download no longer runs next to the activity sync. Both stalled syncs had
   it downloading beside the 0x07 requests. That the overlap causes the stall is not proven (the
   20:00 sync overlapped too and finished), but nothing is lost by running them one after the
   other: a sync now marks the download as owed, and HuaweiSyncState starts it once no sync is
   active. On connect it waits a minute, so a sync that arrives with the connection goes first,
   and two requests within two minutes become one.

3. GetStepDataRequest cast the heart rate, SpO2 and resting heart rate back to byte after
   FitnessData had read them unsigned (0012), so 130 bpm was stored as -126 again. The server held
   six such rows (-127..-109) between 11-14 and 11-21. They are kept as int now; 0xFF still
   means "not measured" (-1).

4. The morning blob retries counted across days, so a long-lived process ran out of them (the
   first attempt on 11-21 was already number 4). The count now starts again each day.

Also: pref_rri_stream_enabled now defaults to false. The nightly blob replaced the stream, and a
cleared preference file must not open it again (an open stream costs the watch 20 % a night).

Compiled: assembleMainlineDebug BUILD_OK. TestFitnessDataSignHandling 4/4 and the new
TestStepDataUnsignedSamples 2/2 pass. Installed 2026-11-22 04:37 (pm install -r): after the
next sync the log shows "FULLDUMP sync idle, downloading now" and the blob downloaded only then;
a second sync 28 s later logged "FULLDUMP skipped". The watchdog reconnect and the heart rate
fix wait for a real stall and a workout.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
